ge over DiLorenzo", "Single late-September UNH poll shows a narrower 4-point race than fundamentals imply", "Markets and most raters put Democrats at Likely; DiLorenzo faces disclosure attacks"], "rationale": "The district leans Democratic by two points, the midterm climate favors Democrats, and Shaheen holds clear financial and outside-spending advantages while DiLorenzo draws negative coverage over his finances. The lone poll shows only a four-point race, so the forecast sits somewhat below the stronger fundamentals rather than above them.", "watch": "Fresh polling or the remaining debates could reveal whether the narrow four-point September survey or the stronger district fundamentals better describe the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Chris Pappas (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Hampshire's 1st District is an open seat after Chris Pappas left it to run for Senate. Stefany Shaheen, daughter of the state's senior senator, faces Republican Anthony DiLorenzo in a district that leans Democratic by only a couple of points but sits in a favorable midterm climate for her party. Most analysts rate the race Likely Democratic, with a few calling it Lean Democratic.\n\nShaheen holds a clear financial edge, with more cash on hand and roughly $2.2 million in outside support, while DiLorenzo has drawn questions about his financial disclosures. The one independent poll, from the University of New Hampshire in late September, showed Shaheen ahead by four points, narrower than broader fundamentals suggest. Betting markets price her chances above 90 percent.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.937, "margin": 10.01}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9238, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9245, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8928, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8695, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.844, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.871, "mar